        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-06-10T23:59:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is not correct, even for Cyan\u0027s part. It depends on SRP1 / SRP0, as well as the WP pin state.",
      "revId": "c3253bb11dbb646a2d90b29d6ae9b69b4f6db4f6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "995834e7_c7872019",
        "filename": "common/spi_flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121520
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-06-11T17:40:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Lets see why this works for Cyan\u0027s W25X40.\n\n1. W25X40 does not have SRP1. It only has SRP0. \n2. W25X40 does not reset SRP0 when HW pin is de-asserted.\n3. The mechanism of SRP/HW is as follows:\n\nW25X10_W25X20_W25X40_W25X80.pdf page 12:\nThe Status Register Protect (SRP) bit is a non-volatile read/write bit in status register (S7) that can be\nused in conjunction with the Write Protect (/WP) pin to disable writes to status register. When the SRP\nbit is set to a 0 state (factory default) the /WP pin has no control over status register. When the SRP\npin is set to a 1, the Write Status Register instruction is locked out while the /WP pin is low. When the\n/WP pin is high the Write Status Register instruction is allowed.\n\nIn other words: when WP is de-asserted, you can change SRP all you like.\n\n4. Please note current code will never be able to change SRP0 because spi_check_flash_wp() actually checks SRP0 state. So this is a catch22! :)\n\n5. The other flash parts namely W25Q64FW does, in fact, reset after power-cycle if SRP0 is 0 and if SRP1  is 1. This is refered to as \"power supply lock-down\" in datasheet. Perhaps the current code works under this assumption?",
      "parentUuid": "39858859_1a44a1c6",
      "revId": "c3253bb11dbb646a2d90b29d6ae9b69b4f6db4f6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "59095cdc_ae646f41",
        "filename": "common/spi_flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-06-12T20:59:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If SRP is zero and the WP pin is asserted, the status register can be changed. But we\u0027d still return ACCESS_DENIED here, which seems incorrect. So we should be checking the WP pin state and SRP state here, just checking the WP pin isn\u0027t enough.",
      "parentUuid": "995834e7_c7872019",
      "revId": "c3253bb11dbb646a2d90b29d6ae9b69b4f6db4f6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
