      "writtenOn": "2015-06-11T17:40:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the problem is that flash_get_protect() earlier sets spi_enable(0) when its done. So this is a clumsy. \n\nI originally wanted to do spi_enable() only in around spi transaction but then I heard this was a bad idea in burst reads cases.\n\nI am not sure what is the best way to deal with this. We can litter this file with spi_enables, but my guess it is not needed on other chips.",
      "parentUuid": "992af412_bd132395",
      "revId": "c3253bb11dbb646a2d90b29d6ae9b69b4f6db4f6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
